message: "If you use this code, please cite the article below."
type: software
title: "Gaussian Splatting for Self-Driving Simulation, Built in Plain PyTorch"
abstract: >-
  3D Gaussian Splatting for driving scenes, implemented entirely in PyTorch
  with no custom CUDA kernels. It reconstructs a PandaSet drive from camera
  and LiDAR data and renders it from the recorded path or from a different lane.
